A YAML outline lists the keys of the root mapping: scalar values print after the key as written (quotes, anchors, aliases), cut after their first line; mappings and lists print only the key, and a key without a value prints as `key:`.
A comment at the key's indentation directly above it starts its line range; one indented deeper belongs to the value above, and trailing comments and blank lines don't end a key's range.
== args
input/ci.yml
== file input/ci.yml
name: CI
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
# The jobs to run.
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    # The steps.

"quoted key": 'single'
script: |
  echo one
  echo two
defaults: &defaults
  shell: bash
copy: *defaults
empty:
? complex
: value
== stdout
input/ci.yml (20 lines)
[L1-L1] name: CI
[L2-L4] on
[L5-L8] jobs
[L11-L11] "quoted key": 'single'
[L12-L14] script: |…
[L15-L16] defaults
[L17-L17] copy: *defaults
[L18-L18] empty:
[L19-L20] complex: value
